ly implemented.\nMandatory half-day design review, checklist, one-page log-schema signed off. That's some changes, reasonably feasible. Could be 3 = some changes, or reasonably feasible measures. Not easy low cost? Half-day per project is cost. Probably 3.\n\nacceptability: degree socially legally politically acceptable.\nCommon strategies that violate no norms. This is acceptable. 4 = common strategies that violate no norms or sensibilities.\n\neffectiveness: degree will solve problem.\nWill it solve logging mandate and/or adapt R&D? Front-loading design prevents rework, ensures logs defined. Reasonable and will contribute to solution but only partial? It addresses design but not technical implementation of automatic recording. Might be partial solution. Effectiveness 3 = reasonable and will contribute to solution of the problem (it helps, but it is only a partial solution). Could be 4 if solves without regard workability? Problem is decide how to meet logging mandate and/or adapt R&D. Defining schema helps meet mandate. Might be partial because doesn't guarantee technical logging works. I'll go 3.\n\napplicability: degree clearly applies to stated problem.\nSolves identified problem directly related. Do X to get Y, Y is part of stated problem. Yes define logging early to meet mandate. That's 4 = solves an identified problem that is directly related.\n\nNeed output format: echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence one sentence then <subscale> integer.\n\nProbably JSON? It says return rating... Provide lines.\n\nLet's produce:\n\nid P1238\noriginality_evidence ... \noriginality 2\netc.\n\nEnsure one sentence evidence.\n\nProceed.\n\n",
