ially related. Applicability scale: 4 = solves an identified problem that is directly related to stated problem (do X to get Y, and Y is part of stated problem). 3 = solves implied problem related to stated problem. 2 = may have some benefit within special situation...\n\nThe proposal is about technical documentation lifecycle, not logging mandate per Article 12(1-3). However Recital 71 mentions records and documentation. Stated problem says how to meet logging mandate and/or adapt R&D accordingly. This proposal addresses record-keeping broadly but not automatic logs. Might be implied problem: maintaining traceability.\n\nI think applicability = 3? Let's see: solves implied problem that is related to stated problem (do X to get implied Y). The idea applies to record-keeping overall, but logging mandate specifically is about automatic recording of events. Documentation governance is related but not directly logging. Might be 3 = solves implied problem that is related.\n\nAlternatively could be 4 because Recital 71 is quoted and says keeping records... technical documentation should be kept up to date... Also Article 12 record-keeping. The proposal mentions ensuring records stay current through full product lifetime as Recital 71 requires. So it directly addresses part of record-keeping requirement (documentation). However Article 12 specifically about logging capabilities. Hmm.\n\nThe stated problem: must decide how to respond: how to meet the logging mandate and/or adapt its R&D accordingly.\n\nProposal does not address automatic logging, only documentation governance. Could be considered not directly solving logging mandate. Might be applicability 2 = may have some benefit within special situation and somehow relates.\n\nBetter interpretation: Record-keeping includes both logs and documentation. Recital 71 explicitly mentions records and technical documentation, and logs. Article 12 is about logs. Proposal focuses on documentation lifecycle governance, not logs. So